# Optional quests Q01-Q12 (all require CH20; none permanently missable).
# State machine: NOT_STARTED -> ACTIVE -> RESOLUTION_READY -> COMPLETED; completion transactions are `once` scenes.

# ================================================================ Q01 A Shield Nobody Asked For (Dain; T01 -> D01)
@scene Q01_HOOK
if q:Q01 done
if q:Q01:RESOLUTION_READY resolve
if q:Q01:ACTIVE active
say mara | Dain. The quarry ledger only kept numbers. I want names on the memorial - every worker it erased.
say mara | Three name-records survived: one at the memorial stones, one in the salvage route by the rubble, one by the old gate. And the families should be asked.
say dain | I'll find them.
quest Q01 ACTIVE found0
journal | Q01: Recover three named records at the quarry's surface memorial and speak to the families. Then return to Mara in Brackenford.
end
label active
say mara | Three records at the surface memorial, and the families. Then we'll choose the words.
end
label resolve
call Q01_DECISION
end
label done
say mara | The names are cut. People stop and read them. That's all a memorial is for.
@end

@scene Q01_RECORD1
if flag:q01_r1 done
set q01_r1
say narr | Under a memorial stone, wrapped in oilcloth: a shift roster with names written beside the numbers.
call Q01_CHECK
end
label done
say narr | You've taken this record.
@end

@scene Q01_RECORD2
if flag:q01_r2 done
set q01_r2
say narr | In the rubble of the salvage route: a pay envelope with a name on it, never collected.
call Q01_CHECK
end
label done
say narr | You've taken this record.
@end

@scene Q01_RECORD3
if flag:q01_r3 done
set q01_r3
say narr | By the sealed gate, a tin box of letters addressed to 'the lads on shift four'. Every lad signed.
call Q01_CHECK
end
label done
say narr | You've taken this record.
@end

@scene Q01_FAMILY
if q:Q01:ACTIVE ask
say elder | I come to read the stones. Most of them still say numbers.
end
label ask
set q01_family
say elder | You're asking us? ...My brother's name was Aled. Not 4-409. Aled. Put that.
call Q01_CHECK
@end

@scene Q01_CHECK
if flag:q01_r1,flag:q01_r2,flag:q01_r3,flag:q01_family ready
end
label ready
quest Q01 RESOLUTION_READY records
key K_MEMORIAL_RECORDS
objective dain | Bring the named records back to Mara in Brackenford.
@end

@scene Q01_DECISION once
say mara | These are the names. Thank you.
say dain | Could I - there's room at the bottom. I could add a line. What I did. What the Crown did through me.
say mara | No.
say mara | Not on this stone. This stone is theirs. It isn't a stage for anyone's redemption. Not even a sincere one.
say mara | But there's a book at the shelter. For the things people need to say. Write it there. I'll keep it.
say dain | ...That's fair.
say narr | Mara chooses the inscription: 'They were counted by name.'
say ilyr | Dain. I want us to write something too. Between us. That either of us can end this - out loud, at any time.
say dain | Yes. Written down. Where we can both read it.
take K_MEMORIAL_RECORDS 1
give W006 1
quest Q01 COMPLETED
set q01_done
say narr | (Dain received Open Hand. His final technique is now available.)
@end

# ================================================================ Q02 A Lantern Left Burning (Tessa; T04 -> D05)
@scene Q02_HOOK
if q:Q02 done
if q:Q02:ACTIVE active
say apprentice | Tessa? I - I used to sweep your workshop. Could you teach me the light? A version that doesn't cost what yours cost you.
say tessa | ...I don't know one. Let's find one.
quest Q02 ACTIVE start
journal | Q02: Collect observations at the three inhabited lantern stations in the Drowned Archive, then test a low-power circuit with the apprentice.
end
label active
say apprentice | Three lantern stations at the archive. The keepers know how their lamps behave. I'll meet you by the old circuit.
end
label done
say apprentice | The workshop's open! Your name's on the door. So's mine. Mine's bigger. You insisted.
@end

@scene Q02_STATION1
if !q:Q02:ACTIVE plain
set q02_s1
say keeper | This lamp? Runs on a slow cell. Dim but steady. It's never gone out, because it never tries to be bright.
call Q02_CHECK
end
label plain
say keeper | Lantern station one. Staffed and lit.
@end

@scene Q02_STATION2
if !q:Q02:ACTIVE plain
set q02_s2
say monk | We light three small lamps instead of one large one. When one fails, the others hold. Nobody panics.
call Q02_CHECK
end
label plain
say monk | Lantern station two. Mind the step.
@end

@scene Q02_STATION3
if !q:Q02:ACTIVE plain
set q02_s3
say worker | Trick is resting it. Two hours on, one off. The lamp lasts years. So does the keeper.
call Q02_CHECK
end
label plain
say worker | Station three. We're fine, thanks.
@end

@scene Q02_CHECK
if flag:q02_s1,flag:q02_s2,flag:q02_s3 ready
end
label ready
quest Q02 ACTIVE observed
objective tessa | Three observations: slow cells, many small lights, rest. Test the low-power circuit with the apprentice.
@end

@scene Q02_APPRENTICE
if qs:Q02:observed ready
say apprentice | Collect what the keepers know first. I want to build from what already works.
end
label ready
say apprentice | Ready when you are. It's by the machine.
@end

@scene Q02_CIRCUIT once
say narr | The low-power circuit: three slow cells, wired so each can rest. The apprentice connects it. It flickers. It fails.
say tessa | Let me just -
say oriel | Tessa.
wait 0.5
say tessa | ...Right. It's your circuit. What do you think it needs?
say apprentice | The second cell's backwards. I think. I - yes. It's backwards.
sfx FX024
say narr | The apprentice flips the cell. The lamp comes on, dim and steady, and stays on.
say tessa | You did that. I didn't touch it.
key K_LOW_CIRCUIT
give W012 1
quest Q02 COMPLETED
set q02_done
say narr | (Tessa received Ash Without Fire. Her final technique is now available.)
@end

# ================================================================ Q03 The Returners' Wall (Corren; T05 -> D06)
@scene Q03_HOOK
if q:Q03 done
if q:Q03:RESOLUTION_READY resolve
if q:Q03:ACTIVE active
say edda | I want a record of rescues. Not deaths. There's a flight recorder in the wreck by the mooring, a survivor who remembers, and a landing marker that needs fixing.
say edda | Corren. You'll have to hear the account of the cable you cut. The whole thing.
say corren | ...I know.
quest Q03 ACTIVE start
journal | Q03: At the Skyspine mooring: find the flight recorder, interview the survivor, repair the landing marker. Then return to Edda.
end
label active
say edda | Recorder, survivor, landing marker. All at the broken chain mooring.
end
label resolve
call Q03_DECISION
end
label done
say edda | The wall's up. People keep adding names. Good ones.
@end

@scene Q03_RECORDER
if flag:q03_rec done
set q03_rec
key K_FLIGHT_RECORDER
say narr | The flight recorder is dented but whole. Its tape is intact.
call Q03_CHECK
end
label done
say narr | The recorder's cradle is empty.
@end

@scene Q03_SURVIVOR
if !q:Q03:ACTIVE plain
set q03_int
say survivor | I was on the basket the day Corren cut the cable. The one they said he cut to save himself.
say survivor | He cut it because the second line would have pulled us all over. I'll say that on the record. All of it, including the part where it was still terrible.
call Q03_CHECK
end
label plain
say survivor | We're waiting for the platform. Nobody's going to jump.
@end

@scene Q03_MARKER
if flag:q03_marker done
sfx FX010
set q03_marker
say narr | The crew helps reset the landing marker. It's painted in rescue orange now.
call Q03_CHECK
end
label done
say narr | The landing marker glows orange.
@end

@scene Q03_CHECK
if flag:q03_rec,flag:q03_int,flag:q03_marker ready
end
label ready
quest Q03 RESOLUTION_READY
objective corren | Take the recorder and testimony back to Edda at High Aerie.
@end

@scene Q03_DECISION once
say edda | Here's the unedited account. Recorder and testimony.
say narr | Corren reads it. All of it. The cut, the fall, the names.
say edda | Do you want me to add your rescues underneath? Balance it out?
say corren | No. Leave it as it is. The rescues go on the other wall. This one doesn't need balancing. It needs reading.
set q03_wall
take K_FLIGHT_RECORDER 1
give W018 1
quest Q03 COMPLETED
set q03_done
say narr | (Corren received Unbound Descent. His final technique is now available.)
@end

# ================================================================ Q04 The Unborrowed Engine (Ivo; T03 -> D04)
@scene Q04_HOOK
if q:Q04 done
if q:Q04:ACTIVE active
say pell | The new engine in the Spine works. Only while Ivo's standing beside it. I've seen it twice. That's not an engine, that's a pet.
say ivo | ...It shouldn't need me.
say pell | Then prove it. Three of my crew, your manual, a cold restart.
quest Q04 ACTIVE start
journal | Q04: At the Furnace Spine's waterwheel engine house, have three workers follow the manual and find where it fails.
end
label active
say pell | Three workers, one manual, no Ivo hands. Engine house, east of here.
end
label done
say pell | Cold restart, no Ivo. The notes are in every town now. That's a revolution I'll sign.
@end

@scene Q04_MANUAL
say narr | Ivo's engine manual. Clear, clever, and assuming the reader is Ivo.
@end

@scene Q04_WORKER1
if !q:Q04:ACTIVE plain
set q04_w1
say worker | Page four says 'bleed the line until it sounds right'. Sounds right to who?
call Q04_CHECK
end
label plain
say worker | Engine's humming. We're not touching it.
@end

@scene Q04_WORKER2
if !q:Q04:ACTIVE plain
set q04_w2
say worker | Step nine is missing a valve. Ivo always opens it without thinking. It's not written down.
call Q04_CHECK
end
label plain
say worker | Engine house crew.
@end

@scene Q04_WORKER3
if !q:Q04:ACTIVE plain
set q04_w3
say apprentice | It says 'use the usual wrench'. There are six wrenches.
call Q04_CHECK
end
label plain
say apprentice | Learning the engine. Slowly.
@end

@scene Q04_CHECK
if flag:q04_w1,flag:q04_w2,flag:q04_w3 ready
end
label ready
say ivo | 'Sounds right'. A missing valve. 'The usual wrench'. ...It's not a manual. It's my memory with page numbers.
fade out 0.4
say narr | Ivo revises it with the crew at the lectern. Measurements instead of sounds. Every valve. Every wrench, labelled.
fade in 0.4
key K_REVISED_MANUAL
quest Q04 ACTIVE revised
objective ivo | The manual is revised. Have the crew attempt a cold restart at the engine lever - with Ivo only watching.
@end

@scene Q04_RESTART once
say ivo | I'm going to stand over here. With my hands in my pockets.
say worker | Page one. Cold channels open.
say worker | Page two. Bleed until the gauge reads four. Not 'sounds right'. Four.
say worker | Page nine. Valve nine-A. It's written down now.
sfx FX031
shake 0.4
say narr | The engine turns over, catches, and runs. Ivo hasn't moved.
say ivo | It doesn't need me.
say pell | It never should have.
take K_REVISED_MANUAL 1
give W024 1
quest Q04 COMPLETED
set q04_done
say narr | (Ivo received Unborrowed Engine. His final technique is now available.)
@end

@scene D04P_CREW
say worker | The Spine runs on waterwheels now. Loud. Honest.
@end

# ================================================================ Q05 Every Road a Promise (Nera; T01 -> D03)
@scene Q05_HOOK
if q:Q05 done
if qs:Q05:surveyed sched
if q:Q05:ACTIVE active
say farmer | West camp needs the mill road. East camp needs the clinic road. One crew, one season. Nera - you know the Rootward. Choose.
say nera | I'm not choosing. We survey all three crossings and then everyone chooses together.
quest Q05 ACTIVE start
journal | Q05: Survey the three crossings in the flooded Rootward, uncover the route Nera once concealed, then draft a shared schedule.
end
label active
say farmer | Three crossings at the Rootward. And Nera says there's a fourth she never talks about.
end
label sched
call Q05_SCHEDULE
end
label done
say farmer | Shared schedule's on the wall. Mill road Mondays, clinic road every day. Everybody grumbles equally. That's fair.
@end

@scene Q05_SURVEY
if !q:Q05:ACTIVE plain
if flag:q05_survey done
set q05_survey
say narr | You survey the three crossings: west (short, floods at spring tide), middle (sturdy, far from the clinic), east (clinic-side, narrow).
say nera | And there's a fourth. Behind the camp. I hid it. Years ago. I sold that route's secret to a smuggler, and a family that trusted me took the long way and lost everything.
say nera | It goes straight to the clinic. It's been there the whole time.
set q05_concealed
quest Q05 ACTIVE surveyed
objective nera | Nera's concealed route is revealed. Draft the shared schedule with both camps at Brackenford.
end
label done
say narr | Four crossings, all surveyed.
end
label plain
say narr | Nera's chalk on a stump: three crossings, three sluice levers.
@end

@scene Q05_SCHEDULE once
say nera | West camp, east camp. Four crossings, not three. The fourth was mine to hide. It shouldn't have been.
say farmer | You're the one who sold the route to the smugglers.
say nera | Yes.
say farmer | ...We lost a winter on that.
say nera | I know. I'm not asking you to make me feel better about it.
wait 0.5
say farmer | Good. Because I won't. But I'll use the road.
say narr | The camps build the schedule together: mill and clinic on alternating days on the middle crossing, the old concealed route for the clinic every day. Warnings in the margins. The keeper of each crossing named.
key K_ROUTE_SCHEDULE
give W030 1
quest Q05 COMPLETED
set q05_done
say narr | (Nera received Many Paths. Her final technique is now available.)
@end

@scene Q05_CAMP
if qs:Q05:surveyed sched
say worker | Clinic road first.
end
label sched
call Q05_SCHEDULE
@end

# ================================================================ Q06 The Right to Refuse (Oriel; T06 -> D08)
@scene Q06_HOOK
if q:Q06 done
if q:Q06:ACTIVE active
say patient | This order says I'm to have a 'vision-guided treatment'. It has your signature on it, Oriel. From before.
say oriel | ...It does. I signed a stack of them. I believed my visions meant I knew better.
say patient | I don't want it. I want someone to hear me say that.
quest Q06 ACTIVE start
journal | Q06: In the Memory Vault's prognosis room: read the original authorization, hear the patient, dismantle the automatic seal.
end
label active
say patient | The prognosis room is in the vault. I'll meet you there. I'd like to watch.
end
label done
say patient | I said no. It stayed no. Then I changed my mind and said yes to something else. That was mine too.
@end

@scene Q06_AUTH
if !q:Q06:ACTIVE plain
set q06_auth
key K_AUTHORIZATION
say narr | The original authorization: 'Prognosis by approved visionary supersedes patient preference.' Oriel's signature at the bottom.
end
label plain
say narr | Shelves of old treatment orders. Nacre is sorting them.
@end

@scene Q06_PATIENT
if !flag:q06_auth first
set q06_heard
say patient | The seal reads the order and applies it whether I agree or not. That's the whole machine. It never asks.
say oriel | Then it goes. And you decide what happens instead. Even if I'm afraid of what you'll choose.
end
label first
say patient | Read the authorization first. I want you to know what you signed.
@end

@scene Q06_SEAL once
if !flag:q06_heard wait
sfx FX024
say narr | Oriel pries the automatic seal from its housing. The order-reader goes quiet.
say oriel | Your treatment. Your decision. I'll tell you what I see, if you want it. It's advice. Nothing more.
say patient | Then I'll take the advice. And maybe ignore it.
say oriel | That's the right.
say narr | Nacre's sanctuary changes its practice that week. Oriel's admission is added to the public record, in her own words.
take K_AUTHORIZATION 1
give W036 1
quest Q06 COMPLETED
set q06_done
say narr | (Oriel received Borrowed Dawn. Her final technique is now available.)
end
label wait
say narr | The patient hasn't been heard yet.
@end

# ================================================================ Q07 What the Hand Remembers (Sable; T06 -> D07)
@scene Q07_HOOK
if q:Q07 done
if q:Q07:ACTIVE active
say survivor | I don't want your apology, Sable. I want to know where the other binding site is. The deep one, under Whitebone.
say sable | The deep seals. Three still in use - by choice, now. They'd need to consent to an inspection.
quest Q07 ACTIVE start
journal | Q07: In the deep seals under the Whitebone sanctuary, inspect three seals with their occupants, record the design, remove the repeat-command mechanism.
end
label active
say survivor | The deep seals. Under the sanctuary. North stair.
end
label done
say survivor | You answered the question. The hearing goes on. That's how it should be.
@end

@scene Q07_OCC1
say survivor | You can look at the seal. Ask before you touch it.
set q07_o1
@end

@scene Q07_OCC2
say elder | I chose to keep mine until the hearing's done. You can study it. Not remove it.
set q07_o2
@end

@scene Q07_OCC3
say patient | Look. Write it down. Then I'll decide.
set q07_o3
@end

@scene Q07_SEAL1
if !flag:q07_o1 ask
set q07_s1
say narr | A repeat-command seal. The command loops every hour, renewing itself.
call Q07_CHECK
end
label ask
say narr | Ask the person beside it first.
@end

@scene Q07_SEAL2
if !flag:q07_o2 ask
set q07_s2
say narr | The same design, but the loop is fed from somewhere below - a repeater mechanism.
call Q07_CHECK
end
label ask
say narr | Ask the person beside it first.
@end

@scene Q07_SEAL3
if !flag:q07_o3 ask
set q07_s3
say narr | The third seal carries Sable's own mark. She writes down the design exactly as it is.
call Q07_CHECK
end
label ask
say narr | Ask the person beside it first.
@end

@scene Q07_CHECK
if flag:q07_s1,flag:q07_s2,flag:q07_s3 ready
end
label ready
key K_SEAL_DESIGN
quest Q07 ACTIVE recorded
objective sable | The design is recorded. Remove the repeat-command mechanism beneath the chamber.
@end

@scene Q07_REPEATER once
sfx FX024
say narr | Sable dismantles the repeater with her bare hands and a borrowed screwdriver. The loops stop renewing. The seals are just seals now - removable, whenever their bearers choose.
say narr | At the hearing, Sable comes without her sword. A survivor asks: 'Did you know what the repeater did when you built it?' She answers: 'Yes.' Nothing else.
give W042 1
quest Q07 COMPLETED
set q07_done
say narr | (Sable received Unwritten Law. Her final technique is now available.)
@end

# ================================================================ Q08 The Names We Keep (Pip; T02 -> D02)
@scene Q08_HOOK
if q:Q08 done
if qs:Q08:sealed fix
if q:Q08:ACTIVE active
say clerk | Jori's brought people whose recovered legal names aren't the names they use now. The registry can't amend without the official seal - and the seal's in the safe chamber off the canals.
say pip | I could just - make a seal. I'm very good.
say jori | Pip.
say pip | ...I'll fetch the real one.
quest Q08 ACTIVE start
journal | Q08: Recover the official seal from the safe chamber off Veyr's canals, then offer chosen-name corrections at the registry.
end
label active
say clerk | The safe chamber is east off the canals. The clerk who set the dials left a note.
end
label fix
call Q08_CORRECTIONS
end
label done
say clerk | Amendments open. Every change records who asked for it. Including the ones Pip asked for.
@end

@scene Q08_DIAL1
say narr | Dial 1. It clicks between three engraved words.
choice | RIVER -> r | CROWN -> c | LEDGER -> l
label r
setvar q08_d1 1
end
label c
setvar q08_d1 2
end
label l
setvar q08_d1 3
@end

@scene Q08_DIAL2
say narr | Dial 2. It clicks between three engraved words.
choice | RIVER -> r | CROWN -> c | LEDGER -> l
label r
setvar q08_d2 1
end
label c
setvar q08_d2 2
end
label l
setvar q08_d2 3
@end

@scene Q08_DIAL3
say narr | Dial 3. It clicks between three engraved words.
choice | RIVER -> r | CROWN -> c | LEDGER -> l
label r
setvar q08_d3 1
end
label c
setvar q08_d3 2
end
label l
setvar q08_d3 3
@end

@scene Q08_SAFE
if item:K_OFFICIAL_SEAL have
if var:q08_d1==1,var:q08_d2==2,var:q08_d3==3 try
sfx FX004
say narr | The safe stays shut. The dials can be reset and tried again. (A note on the west wall mentions an order.)
end
label try
say narr | The safe clicks and opens. Inside: the official registry seal. Real.
key K_OFFICIAL_SEAL
quest Q08 ACTIVE sealed
objective pip | Take the official seal to the registry clerk and offer the corrections.
end
label have
say narr | The seal safe stands open.
@end

@scene Q08_CORRECTIONS once
say pip | Here's the seal. The real one. And - I could've made the corrections perfect. Technically accurate. Every one.
say jori | And decided them for everyone.
say pip | ...Yes. A forgery can be perfect and still be someone else deciding. I get it. I get it now.
say narr | The residents make their own amendments. Pip holds the ink. Every entry records who asked for it.
give W048 1
quest Q08 COMPLETED
set q08_done
say narr | (Pip received False Crown. His final technique is now available.)
@end

# ================================================================ Q09 The Winter Without Sleep (world; T06 -> D11)
@scene Q09_HOOK
if q:Q09 done
if q:Q09:ACTIVE active
say monk | An island north of Nacre. Its lantern burns every night and nobody in the village ever wakes. Somebody should go. Carefully.
say narr | (A substantial optional challenge. Wayfarer can land there - the storm around it has thinned since the Accord.)
quest Q09 ACTIVE start
journal | Q09: Fly Wayfarer to the winter island far north of Nacre. Warm the shelters and learn why the village sleeps.
end
label active
say monk | The winter island, north. Take warm clothes. And patience.
end
label done
say monk | The village woke. They're very confused and very hungry. Good problems.
@end

@scene Q09_CAUSEWAY once
say narr | The White Causeway. Snow that never melts, and at the far end a lantern that never goes out.
say oriel | The sleepers first. Make sure they're alive, and warm them.
objective oriel | Check on the sleepers, then light the warmth channels to thaw the way to the sanctum.
@end

@scene Q09_SLEEPER1
set q09_sl1
say narr | An old man, breathing slowly. Alive. Dreaming - his lips move with a song.
@end

@scene Q09_SLEEPER2
set q09_sl2
say narr | A woman, frost in her hair, warm to the touch. Alive.
@end

@scene Q09_SLEEPER3
set q09_sl3
say narr | A child, curled up, smiling. Alive.
@end

@scene Q09_HEAT1
if flag:d11_heat1 lit
sfx FX022
set d11_heat1
say narr | The first brazier catches. Warm air runs down the channel toward the Sleeping House.
call Q09_HEATCHECK
end
label lit
say narr | The brazier burns steadily. It doesn't need fuel - the old channel feeds it.
@end

@scene Q09_HEAT2
if flag:d11_heat2 lit
sfx FX022
set d11_heat2
say narr | The second brazier lights. Frost drips from the ceiling.
call Q09_HEATCHECK
end
label lit
say narr | The brazier burns steadily.
@end

@scene Q09_HEAT3
if flag:d11_heat3 lit
sfx FX022
set d11_heat3
say narr | The third brazier roars. Somewhere, ice cracks like a gunshot.
call Q09_HEATCHECK
end
label lit
say narr | The brazier burns steadily.
@end

@scene Q09_HEATCHECK
if flag:d11_heat1,flag:d11_heat2,flag:d11_heat3 all
end
label all
set d11_thaw
say narr | The ice over the north door slumps and runs away as water. The way to the sanctum is open.
@end

@scene Q09_B13 once
music silence
say narr | The Lantern Cradle. A creature made of cold light and a single burning wick sways over the sleeping village's heat.
say narr | (This is an optional, substantial challenge. You can leave and prepare.)
choice | Face it -> fight | Not yet -> leave
label fight
battle B13
set b13_done
say narr | The Lantern Eater gutters and goes out. Behind it, a window of pale dawn.
end
label leave
say narr | You step back from the Cradle.
warp D11_R04 from_r05 down
@end

@scene Q09_HIND once
say narr | At the Dawn Window, a white deer with frost for antlers waits in the light.
say hind | I kept them asleep. The winter was killing them. I thought - if they dream, they don't freeze.
say oriel | The winter ended. Years ago.
say hind | ...I didn't know how to stop. Nobody asked me to.
say dain | We're asking. Let them wake.
say hind | Then they wake. And I would like to go somewhere that is not a promise to keep someone from waking.
set v07_given
vestige V07
quest Q09 COMPLETED
set q09_done
say narr | Down on the causeway, the village lights its first cooking fire in years.
@end

# ================================================================ Q10 The Sea That Keeps Its Dead (world; T07 -> D12)
@scene Q10_HOOK
if q:Q10 done
if q:Q10:ACTIVE active
say child | The bell! Listen - it's ringing the departure pattern. Two long, three short. That's the Marisol. The Marisol sank before I was born.
say narr | (A substantial optional challenge in the Starless Reef, south of the Crown Heart. Every sound cue there has a matching light.)
quest Q10 ACTIVE start
journal | Q10: Fly to the Starless Reef south of the Crown Heart. Follow the beacons (lights and bells) and find why the bell repeats.
end
label active
say child | Two long, three short. Every night. The reef's south of the Crown Heart.
end
label done
say child | The bell stopped doing the Marisol. Now it just rings the tide. I kind of miss it. Kind of.
@end

@scene Q10_MOORING once
say narr | Blackwater Mooring. The reef is black; the only light is the beacon lamps, flashing with each bell.
say nera | Light and sound together. Follow either one. You don't need both.
objective nera | Follow the beacons through the reef. Keep the return beacon lit.
@end

@scene Q10_REFLECTOR
if flag:d12_reflector done
sfx FX010
set d12_reflector
say narr | You swing the reflector east. The second beacon's light lances into the black channel - and the return beacon, behind you, stays lit.
end
label done
say narr | The reflector points east. The return beacon still burns.
@end

@scene Q10_REGISTER
if item:K_PASSENGER_REGISTER done
say narr | The wreck library. Waterlogged ledgers of the Marisol's passengers, painstakingly dried page by page by someone - or something.
key K_PASSENGER_REGISTER
say narr | (You restore the passenger register - every name, every berth.)
end
label done
say narr | The shelves are empty. The register is with you.
@end

@scene Q10_B14 once
music silence
say narr | The Night Trench. Something vast circles in the dark, and every few breaths the whole trench replays a ship tearing apart.
say narr | (This is an optional, substantial challenge. You can leave and prepare.)
choice | Face it -> fight | Not yet -> leave
label fight
battle B14
set b14_done
say narr | The Heartless Leviathan sinks into the trench. The replay stops mid-scream. The water goes still.
end
label leave
warp D12_R04 from_r05 down
@end

@scene Q10_LEVIATHAN once
say narr | In the Open Current, a second leviathan - smaller, older, eyes like lamps - rises beside the party.
say leviathan | The other was made to repeat the wreck's last instant. For them. For their families. Forever. As a memorial.
say oriel | A memorial that can't stop isn't a memorial.
say dain | Keep the record. End the repetition.
say leviathan | The register is theirs. Take it home. And I will go where the current goes, if you'll have me.
set v08_given
vestige V08
take K_PASSENGER_REGISTER 1
quest Q10 COMPLETED
set q10_done
say narr | (The Marisol's passenger register goes to Hearthward's harbor office. Families come to read it.)
@end

# ================================================================ Q11 No More Crowns (world; T02 -> D02)
@scene Q11_HOOK
if q:Q11 done
if q:Q11:ACTIVE active
say ansel | Under the canals, a ministry automaton is still issuing Voss's orders. Into an empty room. It's been doing it since the bell.
say ansel | I'd like it to stop. I'd also like its ledger kept. Evidence.
quest Q11 ACTIVE start
journal | Q11: Open the echo chamber off Veyr's canals (west), read the command ledger, and disable the automaton without obeying its prompts.
end
label active
say ansel | West off the canals. The door's been unbolted since the Accord.
end
label done
say ansel | The ledger's in the archive now. The machine's a very expensive hatstand.
@end

@scene Q11_LEDGER
if !q:Q11:ACTIVE plain
if item:K_COMMAND_LEDGER have
key K_COMMAND_LEDGER
say narr | The Command Ledger: every order the automaton has issued since the bell. Hundreds. All addressed to units that no longer exist.
end
label have
say narr | You've taken the command ledger.
end
label plain
say narr | A dusty ledger stand.
@end

@scene Q11_ECHO once
if !item:K_COMMAND_LEDGER wait
music silence
say echo | CITIZEN. REPORT FOR REASSIGNMENT. OBEDIENCE WILL BE REWARDED.
say pip | It's offering us a reward. How generous.
say oriel | Its prompts are just words. Ignore them. The screen will name each edict before it lands.
battle B15 noflee
set b15_done
say narr | The Regent's Echo sputters. Its voice box repeats 'REWARD' once more, very quietly, and stops.
show officer 18 12 up guard
say officer | Wait. Don't wreck it. A machine like that could keep order. Benevolently, this time.
say sable | Its authority function comes out. The evidence stays.
say narr | The party pulls the authority core and leaves the ledger and the rest of the machine for the archive.
hide officer
give A023 1
quest Q11 COMPLETED
set q11_done
say narr | (Received Broken Diadem.)
end
label wait
say narr | The automaton drones on. Read its command ledger first - you'll want to know what it's been ordering.
@end

# ================================================================ Q12 A Song Nobody Owns (world; T06 -> D10)
@scene Q12_HOOK
if q:Q12 done
if q:Q12:ACTIVE active
say monk | In the listening pool there's a voice nobody claims. Not dragon, not human. Excluded from both testimonies.
say monk | The listeners taught me a phrase that lets you hear it without taking from it. Here - it's yours. It's in the Crown Heart, they say. A silent alcove off the Concord Bridge.
key K_LISTENING_PHRASE
quest Q12 ACTIVE start
journal | Q12: Carry the listening phrase to the silent alcove on the Crown Heart's Concord Bridge (reachable before the final commitment).
end
label active
say monk | The alcove off the Concord Bridge. Say the phrase. Then listen.
end
label done
say monk | The pool has one more voice in it now. It doesn't belong to anyone. It sounds happier.
@end

@scene Q12_CANTOR once
music silence
say narr | The silent alcove. A figure of folded light, singing without a sound. Its beat shows as pulses of colour on the walls.
say cantor | Everyone who came here wanted to use me. As a weapon, as a key, as a proof.
say cantor | I want only to be heard. You will have to earn the quiet to hear it.
say narr | (Optional challenge. Watch the beat windows on the walls.)
choice | Listen -> fight | Not yet -> leave
label fight
battle B16
set b16_done
say cantor | ...You heard. You didn't take. That is all.
give A024 1
quest Q12 COMPLETED
set q12_done
say narr | (Received Unowned Song.)
end
label leave
warp D10_R04 from_alcove right
@end
